meta {
  name: Admin looks up a customer
  type: http
  seq: 8
  tags: [
    customer
    manual
  ]
}

get {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/customers/{{CUSTOMER_ID}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN}}
}

docs {
  No automated assertion here on purpose — this request only returns 200 after
  the manual setup below; anything else (401 with ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN still
  empty, for example) is expected until you do it, not a bug.

  Manual setup — there is no self-service way to become ADMIN yet:

  1. Run "Register customer", then grant the ADMIN profile directly in Postgres:
     INSERT INTO usuarios_perfis (usuario_id, perfil_id)
     VALUES ('{{CUSTOMER_ID}}', '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002')
     ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
  2. Run "Login customer" again so the new token's "profiles" claim includes ADMIN.
  3. Paste that accessToken into the ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN environment variable.
  4. Run this request.
}
